(window.XZ_MANUAL_CHAPTERS=window.XZ_MANUAL_CHAPTERS||{})["four-decks"]="<header class=\"mc-head\"><p class=\"mc-eyebrow\">On the player<\/p><h2 class=\"mc-title\" tabindex=\"-1\">Four decks<\/h2><p class=\"mc-lede\">Playing decks 3 and 4 over the loopback cable: setup, deck view, what decks 3 and 4 can do, and every status.<\/p><p class=\"applies\" data-applies=\"both\">Applies to <b>MODERN and CLASSIC<\/b><\/p><\/header><p>Four decks adds two software players, DECK 3 and DECK 4, to the XDJ-XZ's own DECK 1 and DECK 2. You hear them on mixer channels CH3 and CH4. A short USB cable from the back of the player to a top USB port carries their sound into the mixer: it leaves through USB 1 on top and comes back in at the rear USB socket, where a computer with DJ software would connect. The physical controls switch between decks with the same presses DJ software uses on the XDJ-XZ.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mx\" data-mx=\"loopback-signal\" data-mode=\"scenes\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"How the sound of decks 3 and 4 reaches the mixer\"><ol class=\"mx-scenes\"><li data-title=\"Decks 3 and 4\"><b>Decks 3 and 4<\/b> <span>Decks 3 and 4 are software players. They run inside the player, beside decks 1 and 2.<\/span><\/li><li data-title=\"USB 1\"><b>USB 1<\/b> <span>Their sound leaves the player through USB 1 on the top panel.<\/span><\/li><li data-title=\"Loopback cable\"><b>Loopback cable<\/b> <span>The loopback cable carries it over the back edge of the player.<\/span><\/li><li data-title=\"Rear USB\"><b>Rear USB<\/b> <span>It comes back in at the rear USB socket, where a computer with DJ software would connect.<\/span><\/li><li data-title=\"CH3 and CH4\"><b>CH3 and CH4<\/b> <span>With their input switches on USB, mixer channels CH3 and CH4 play decks 3 and 4.<\/span><\/li><\/ol><\/div>\n<aside class=\"callout callout--experimental\"><b>Experimental<\/b><p>Four decks is experimental in this version. Test it with your own tracks before a set, keep the music stick connected, and keep a two-deck plan ready.<\/p><\/aside>\n<h3 id=\"m-what-you-need\" data-anchor=\"what-you-need\">What you need <span class=\"tag tag--experimental\">experimental<\/span><\/h3>\n<ul><li>The <strong>loopback cable<\/strong>: a USB cable with a USB-B plug on one end and a USB-A plug on the other, the kind a printer uses.<\/li><li>Your <strong>music stick<\/strong> in the other top USB port. Decks 3 and 4 read their tracks from it.<\/li><li>Decks 1 and 2 <strong>stopped or paused<\/strong> while decks 3 and 4 start. Once they run, you can play all four decks.<\/li><li><strong>CH3<\/strong> and <strong>CH4<\/strong> on the mixer set to <strong>USB<\/strong> so you hear decks 3 and 4.<\/li><\/ul>\n<p>The cable goes from the rear USB socket to a top USB port. In this version the screens name <strong>USB 1<\/strong> for the cable and <strong>USB 2<\/strong> for the music stick. Use those ports.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mx\" data-mx=\"loopback-cable\" data-mode=\"video\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"The loopback cable\"><ol class=\"mx-scenes\"><li data-title=\"One USB-B to USB-A cable runs from the rear USB socket over the back edge into USB 1 on top. No computer is involved.\"><b>One USB-B to USB-A cable runs from the rear USB socket over the back edge into USB 1 on top. No computer is involved.<\/b> <span>One USB-B to USB-A cable runs from the rear USB socket over the back edge into USB 1 on top. No computer is involved.<\/span><\/li><\/ol><\/div>\n<h3 id=\"m-set-up-four-decks\" data-anchor=\"set-up-four-decks\">Set up four decks <span class=\"tag tag--experimental\">experimental<\/span><\/h3>\n<div class=\"mx\" data-mx=\"four-deck-setup\" data-mode=\"steps\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Set up four decks, step by step\"><\/div>\n<ol class=\"steps\"><li>Stop or pause decks 1 and 2.<\/li><li>Put your music stick in <strong>USB 2<\/strong> on the top panel.<\/li><li>Plug the USB-B end of the loopback cable into the <strong>rear USB socket<\/strong>.<\/li><li>Plug the USB-A end into <strong>USB 1<\/strong> on the top panel.<\/li><li>Set the <strong>CH3<\/strong> and <strong>CH4<\/strong> input switches to <strong>USB<\/strong>.<\/li><li>Tap <strong>DECKS<\/strong> at the top of the play screen and choose one of the <strong>4 DECKS<\/strong> pictures, or open MODS and choose <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"mods-menu\" data-anchor=\"4-decks\">4 DECKS<\/a>.<\/li><li>Wait for <strong>DECKS 3 AND 4 ARE READY<\/strong>. The card in the lanes of decks 3 and 4 tells you each step it is waiting for.<\/li><li>Press <kbd>SHIFT<\/kbd> twice on the left side to play deck 3, or on the right side to play deck 4.<\/li><\/ol>\n<p>The XZ keeps looking for the cable on its own. You never have to restart anything. <strong>RESCAN<\/strong> checks at once.<\/p>\n<aside class=\"callout callout--tip\"><b>Tip<\/b><p>You can choose a four-deck view before you plug in the cable. Decks 3 and 4 then show a card with the cable steps and their current state, and decks 1 and 2 keep playing as usual.<\/p><\/aside>\n<h3 id=\"m-the-4-decks-page-in-mods\" data-anchor=\"the-4-decks-page-in-mods\">The 4 DECKS page in MODS<\/h3>\n<p>MODS &gt; <strong>4 DECKS<\/strong> shows the cable's state, lets you choose the deck view, and lists what works on each deck.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-four-decks-1\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODS · 4 DECKS<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/8b91f24c147a0424.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"The 4 DECKS page before the cable is plugged in. In this picture the key and RAM engines have not reported yet, so KEY SYNC has no tick on decks 1 and 2 and RAM TRACKS none on any deck.\" data-iface=\"modern\"><img src=\"manual/shots/a46c7c642b0898ff.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"The 4 DECKS page before the cable is plugged in. In this picture the key and RAM engines have not reported yet, so KEY SYNC has no tick on decks 1 and 2 and RAM TRACKS none on any deck.\" data-iface=\"classic\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"17.250\" data-y=\"12.083\" aria-label=\"1: Cable picture\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-1-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"42.500\" data-y=\"13.958\" aria-label=\"2: State\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-1-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"77.500\" data-y=\"22.917\" aria-label=\"3: RESCAN\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-1-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"16.000\" data-y=\"37.083\" aria-label=\"4: DECK VIEW\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-1-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"55.250\" data-y=\"43.333\" aria-label=\"5: Deck columns\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-1-5\">5<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"6\" data-x=\"16.000\" data-y=\"49.583\" aria-label=\"6: Feature row\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-1-6\">6<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"7\" data-x=\"15.000\" data-y=\"88.542\" aria-label=\"7: Dock\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-1-7\">7<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"8\" data-x=\"89.000\" data-y=\"88.542\" aria-label=\"8: Save state\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-1-8\">8<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>The 4 DECKS page before the cable is plugged in. In this picture the key and RAM engines have not reported yet, so KEY SYNC has no tick on decks 1 and 2 and RAM TRACKS none on any deck.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-four-decks-1-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>Cable picture<\/b> <span>Shows the cable going from USB 1 on top to the rear USB socket. The part that needs you is marked in the state's colour.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-four-decks-1-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>State<\/b> <span>Where four decks stand now, with one sentence on what happens next. The states are listed under <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"four-decks\" data-anchor=\"the-card-in-every-state\">The card in every state<\/a>.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-four-decks-1-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>RESCAN<\/b> <span>Checks the cable and the audio route now. Reads TRY AGAIN after a failed start and SCANNING while a check runs.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-four-decks-1-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>DECK VIEW<\/b> <span>2 DECKS, 4 DECKS in number order (1 2 3 4) or 4 DECKS in mixer order (3 1 2 4). The highlighted box is the saved view.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-four-decks-1-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>Deck columns<\/b> <span>One column per deck, in mixer order 3 1 2 4, the same on both halves of the grid.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"6\" id=\"f-four-decks-1-6\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">6<\/span><div><b>Feature row<\/b> <span>A tick means the feature works on that deck. A dash means it does not. Turn the encoder onto a row and the dock says why.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"7\" id=\"f-four-decks-1-7\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">7<\/span><div><b>Dock<\/b> <span>Explains the highlighted control or row.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"8\" id=\"f-four-decks-1-8\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">8<\/span><div><b>Save state<\/b> <span>Confirms that your deck view is saved to the USB.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<p>The HOME page shows the same state on the 4 DECKS card. When four decks need you (no cable found, a failed start, a lost connection, or no four-deck engine on the USB loader) HOME also shows <strong>SET UP FOUR DECKS<\/strong>, which opens this page.<\/p>\n<p>If the USB loader has no four-deck engine, the page says so and offers <strong>CHECK INSTALLED ENGINE<\/strong>. Rebuild the USB loader in the <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"desktop-app\">XZ Mods app<\/a>, restart the player with it, then press <strong>CHECK INSTALLED ENGINE<\/strong>.<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>HOME status line<\/th><th>What it means<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>Not connected<\/td><td>No loopback cable found yet.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Looking for the cable<\/td><td>A check is running now.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Starting decks 3 and 4<\/td><td>The cable is found and the software players are starting, or they wait for decks 1 and 2 to stop.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Ready, 2 decks shown<\/td><td>Decks 3 and 4 run. The play screen shows two decks.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Ready, 4 decks shown<\/td><td>Decks 3 and 4 run. The play screen shows four decks.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Could not start<\/td><td>The start failed. The 4 DECKS page says why.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Disconnected<\/td><td>The cable was unplugged or lost power.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Not available on this player<\/td><td>The software players are not running in this build.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<h3 id=\"m-the-card-in-every-state\" data-anchor=\"the-card-in-every-state\">The card in every state<\/h3>\n<p>While decks 3 and 4 are not running, a four-deck view puts a card in their lanes. The card shows the cable steps, the state, and the buttons you need. Decks 1 and 2 stay live above it. In number order the card fills the lanes of decks 3 and 4 under decks 1 and 2. In mixer order it splits into a strip above deck 1 and a strip below deck 2.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-four-decks-2\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">Play screen · NO CABLE FOUND<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/1b9a018855ca895f.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Four decks in number order before the cable is plugged in. CLASSIC draws the same card in its own colours, with shorter sentences.\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"30.000\" data-y=\"55.417\" aria-label=\"1: Cable picture\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-2-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"83.125\" data-y=\"42.292\" aria-label=\"2: Steps\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-2-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"35.250\" data-y=\"58.958\" aria-label=\"3: State\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-2-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"59.375\" data-y=\"62.292\" aria-label=\"4: RESCAN\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-2-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"90.000\" data-y=\"55.417\" aria-label=\"5: TWO DECKS\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-2-5\">5<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"6\" data-x=\"10.250\" data-y=\"50.000\" aria-label=\"6: Deck 3 tag\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-2-6\">6<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"7\" data-x=\"18.750\" data-y=\"85.417\" aria-label=\"7: Deck 3 channel\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-2-7\">7<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"8\" data-x=\"79.625\" data-y=\"2.500\" aria-label=\"8: DECKS button\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-2-8\">8<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>Four decks in number order before the cable is plugged in. CLASSIC draws the same card in its own colours, with shorter sentences.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-four-decks-2-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>Cable picture<\/b> <span>The cable from USB 1 on top to the rear USB socket. It moves for a minute after the card appears or after your last input, then rests.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-four-decks-2-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>Steps<\/b> <span>The two things to do: connect the cable, and set the CH3 and CH4 input switches to USB.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-four-decks-2-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>State<\/b> <span>The state's title and what happens next.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-four-decks-2-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>RESCAN<\/b> <span>Checks for the cable now.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-four-decks-2-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>TWO DECKS<\/b> <span>Goes back to the two-deck view. Decks 3 and 4 keep trying in the background.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"6\" id=\"f-four-decks-2-6\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">6<\/span><div><b>Deck 3 tag<\/b> <span>NOT CONNECTED while deck 3 is not running.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"7\" id=\"f-four-decks-2-7\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">7<\/span><div><b>Deck 3 channel<\/b> <span>The bottom channel of deck 3 waits for the loopback cable.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"8\" id=\"f-four-decks-2-8\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">8<\/span><div><b>DECKS button<\/b> <span>Shows the current view. The small amber dot means decks 3 and 4 are not connected.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<p>You can drive the card with the encoder. While the card shows, push the encoder to highlight <strong>RESCAN<\/strong>, turn it to move between the card's buttons and the <strong>DECKS<\/strong> button, and push again to press. <kbd>BACK<\/kbd>, or six seconds without input, gives the encoder back to the player.<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Card title<\/th><th>What it means<\/th><th>What to do<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>NO CABLE FOUND<\/td><td>The XZ does not see the loopback cable.<\/td><td>Plug in the cable as in the steps. Keep the music stick in USB 2. Press <strong>RESCAN<\/strong> to check at once.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>LOOKING FOR THE CABLE...<\/td><td>A check runs now. The button reads <strong>SCANNING<\/strong>.<\/td><td>Wait a moment.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>STARTING DECKS 3 AND 4<\/td><td>The cable is found and the audio input is starting.<\/td><td>Wait a few seconds. The card's sentence says which step is running.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>STOP DECKS 1 AND 2<\/td><td>Decks 3 and 4 start only while decks 1 and 2 are both stopped.<\/td><td>Stop or pause decks 1 and 2. The card changes by itself.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>COULD NOT START DECKS 3 AND 4<\/td><td>The start failed. The picture marks the part that failed in red: USB 1, the cable, the rear socket or the CH3/CH4 switches.<\/td><td>Read the sentence, fix that part, then press <strong>TRY AGAIN<\/strong>.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>DECKS 3 AND 4 DISCONNECTED<\/td><td>The cable was unplugged or lost power while decks 3 and 4 ran.<\/td><td>Plug the cable back in and press <strong>RESCAN<\/strong>.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>FOUR DECKS ARE NOT AVAILABLE<\/td><td>The software players are not running in this build. Decks 1 and 2 play as usual.<\/td><td>Press <strong>TWO DECKS<\/strong>.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>DECKS 3 AND 4 ARE READY<\/td><td>The route came up. The card turns green, then wipes away.<\/td><td>Press <kbd>SHIFT<\/kbd> twice on a side to play deck 3 or 4.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-four-decks-3\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/97c3b69432d2782a.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: LOOKING FOR THE CABLE. A check is running, so the button reads SCANNING\"><img src=\"manual/shots/97c3b69432d2782a.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>LOOKING FOR THE CABLE. A check is running, so the button reads SCANNING<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/a1eed35b30bb1338.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: STARTING DECKS 3 AND 4. The cable is found and the audio input is starting\"><img src=\"manual/shots/a1eed35b30bb1338.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>STARTING DECKS 3 AND 4. The cable is found and the audio input is starting<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/1f5ba1f3a1eabff1.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: STOP DECKS 1 AND 2, in mixer order. The card splits into two strips\"><img src=\"manual/shots/1f5ba1f3a1eabff1.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>STOP DECKS 1 AND 2, in mixer order. The card splits into two strips<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/de996191f2b20f13.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: COULD NOT START. The failed part is marked in red and the button reads TRY AGAIN\"><img src=\"manual/shots/de996191f2b20f13.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>COULD NOT START. The failed part is marked in red and the button reads TRY AGAIN<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/7da11420439cb6e7.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: DECKS 3 AND 4 DISCONNECTED. The cable went away while decks 3 and 4 ran\"><img src=\"manual/shots/7da11420439cb6e7.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>DECKS 3 AND 4 DISCONNECTED. The cable went away while decks 3 and 4 ran<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/1a02551dead14400.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: FOUR DECKS ARE NOT AVAILABLE. Only TWO DECKS is offered\"><img src=\"manual/shots/1a02551dead14400.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>FOUR DECKS ARE NOT AVAILABLE. Only TWO DECKS is offered<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/d32faa0b801234c1.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: NO CABLE FOUND in mixer order\"><img src=\"manual/shots/d32faa0b801234c1.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>NO CABLE FOUND in mixer order<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/61c367e79a527913.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: The encoder on the card. RESCAN is highlighted\"><img src=\"manual/shots/61c367e79a527913.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>The encoder on the card. RESCAN is highlighted<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/459eadd57f22ca60.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: DECKS 3 AND 4 ARE READY. The card turns green\"><img src=\"manual/shots/459eadd57f22ca60.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>DECKS 3 AND 4 ARE READY. The card turns green<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/fddcd4db20a68e72.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: The card wipes away and decks 3 and 4 appear\"><img src=\"manual/shots/fddcd4db20a68e72.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>The card wipes away and decks 3 and 4 appear<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<p>When the route comes up, a banner says <strong>DECKS 3 AND 4 ARE READY<\/strong> for a few seconds. If the play screen shows two decks at that moment, the banner says <strong>DECKS 3 AND 4 ARE READY. TAP DECKS AT THE TOP FOR FOUR DECKS.<\/strong> The view does not change by itself.<\/p>\n<h4 id=\"m-the-e-8307-hub-warning\" data-anchor=\"the-e-8307-hub-warning\">The E-8307 hub warning <span class=\"tag tag--experimental\">experimental<\/span><\/h4>\n<p>The player sees the loopback cable as a USB hub. When you plug it in, the player raises its own warning <strong>E-8307: HUBS ARE NOT SUPPORTED<\/strong> and keeps it up while the cable stays in. That is not an error, so XZ Mods never shows it, whether four decks are on or not.<\/p>\n<ul><li>MODERN and MODS show nothing and keep working as usual.<\/li><li>In CLASSIC the player's own warning window turns into a calm card: <strong>LOOPBACK CABLE CONNECTED<\/strong>, <strong>USED BY DECKS 3 AND 4 · NOT AN ERROR<\/strong>.<\/li><\/ul>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-four-decks-4\" data-iface=\"classic\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/42ec366b670b5b0c.webp\" data-w=\"304\" data-h=\"60\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: The player&#x27;s window with the loopback cable in\"><img src=\"manual/shots/42ec366b670b5b0c.webp\" width=\"304\" height=\"60\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>The player's window with the loopback cable in<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/441e64b0769c0f6f.webp\" data-w=\"420\" data-h=\"100\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: The same card in a larger window\"><img src=\"manual/shots/441e64b0769c0f6f.webp\" width=\"420\" height=\"100\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>The same card in a larger window<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<p>If a USB hub or another device the player does not support is in a top USB port, the player cannot use it either. Plug music sticks straight into a top port.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-deck-view\" data-anchor=\"deck-view\">DECK VIEW<\/h3>\n<p>DECK VIEW chooses what the play screen shows. It changes neither the sound, the mixer channels, nor which deck a side controls.<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>DECK VIEW<\/th><th>Waveform lanes, top to bottom<\/th><th>Bottom channels<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>2 DECKS (the default)<\/td><td>The two decks the sides control<\/td><td>The same two decks<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>4 DECKS, number order 1 2 3 4<\/td><td>1, 2, 3, 4<\/td><td>3, 1, 2, 4<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>4 DECKS, mixer order 3 1 2 4<\/td><td>3, 1, 2, 4<\/td><td>3, 1, 2, 4<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>The bottom channels always follow the mixer, left to right: CH3, CH1, CH2, CH4. Mixer order puts the lanes in the same order, top to bottom. Each lane and each channel carries its deck's number in a badge, so you can always tell which deck is which. Decks 1 and 2 have a white number on grey. Decks 3 and 4 have a black number on white, as on the jog displays.<\/p>\n<p>DECK VIEW is saved to the USB with your other settings. You can change it in five places, and they all change the same setting:<\/p>\n<ul><li>the <strong>DECKS<\/strong> button at the top of the play screen;<\/li><li><strong>TWO DECKS<\/strong> on the card;<\/li><li>MODS &gt; <strong>SCREEN<\/strong> &gt; <strong>DECK VIEW<\/strong>;<\/li><li>MODS &gt; <strong>4 DECKS<\/strong> &gt; <strong>DECK VIEW<\/strong>;<\/li><li>the button next to LINK, when you set it to <strong>DECK VIEW<\/strong> in MODS &gt; PLAY &gt; <strong>BUTTON NEXT TO LINK<\/strong>. Each press then steps 2 DECKS, 4 DECKS in number order, 4 DECKS in mixer order.<\/li><\/ul>\n<h4 id=\"m-the-decks-button-and-its-picker\" data-anchor=\"the-decks-button-and-its-picker\">The DECKS button and its picker<\/h4>\n<p>The <strong>DECKS<\/strong> button is always at the top of the play screen in both interfaces. It names the decks on screen: <strong>DECKS 1 2<\/strong>, <strong>DECKS 1234<\/strong>, <strong>DECKS 3124<\/strong>, or the pair the sides control in 2 DECKS, such as <strong>DECKS 3 2<\/strong>. In MODERN it sits left of the INFO button. In CLASSIC it sits in the black space between VJ.TOOLS and the METRICS readout.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-four-decks-5\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">DECK VIEW picker<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/adf319ed006389f9.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Tap DECKS to open the picker. Tap a picture to choose it.\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"79.625\" data-y=\"2.500\" aria-label=\"1: DECKS button\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-5-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"52.500\" data-y=\"38.542\" aria-label=\"2: 2 DECKS\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-5-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"71.875\" data-y=\"34.375\" aria-label=\"3: 4 DECKS, number order\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-5-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"92.500\" data-y=\"34.375\" aria-label=\"4: 4 DECKS, mixer order\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-5-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"77.250\" data-y=\"39.167\" aria-label=\"5: Status\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-5-5\">5<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>Tap DECKS to open the picker. Tap a picture to choose it.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-four-decks-5-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>DECKS button<\/b> <span>Opens and closes the picker. It shows the view now on screen.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-four-decks-5-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>2 DECKS<\/b> <span>The two decks the sides control, like the player itself.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-four-decks-5-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>4 DECKS, number order<\/b> <span>All four decks, lanes 1 2 3 4.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-four-decks-5-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>4 DECKS, mixer order<\/b> <span>All four decks, lanes 3 1 2 4, matching the mixer channels.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-four-decks-5-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>Status<\/b> <span>LIKE THE PLAYER ITSELF for two decks. DECKS 3 AND 4 READY in green, or 3 AND 4 NOT CONNECTED in amber.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<p>A tap outside the picker, <kbd>BACK<\/kbd>, or six seconds without input closes it. The encoder also turns and pushes inside the open picker.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-four-decks-6\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/c36b7163962dd08a.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: 2 DECKS. The player&#x27;s own two-deck screen with the DECKS button at the top\"><img src=\"manual/shots/c36b7163962dd08a.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>2 DECKS. The player's own two-deck screen with the DECKS button at the top<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/11eedfd82f73b04d.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: 4 DECKS in number order with decks 3 and 4 ready\"><img src=\"manual/shots/11eedfd82f73b04d.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>4 DECKS in number order with decks 3 and 4 ready<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/1f40f781792e3958.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: 4 DECKS in mixer order. Lanes 3 1 2 4 over channels 3 1 2 4\"><img src=\"manual/shots/1f40f781792e3958.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>4 DECKS in mixer order. Lanes 3 1 2 4 over channels 3 1 2 4<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/946b1ad9bf0df5a8.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: 2 DECKS with the left side on deck 3. The screen shows decks 3 and 2\"><img src=\"manual/shots/946b1ad9bf0df5a8.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>2 DECKS with the left side on deck 3. The screen shows decks 3 and 2<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/f24db97ffb292d21.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: 2 DECKS when decks 3 and 4 come up. The banner says how to show four\"><img src=\"manual/shots/f24db97ffb292d21.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>2 DECKS when decks 3 and 4 come up. The banner says how to show four<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<h3 id=\"m-switch-a-side-between-decks\" data-anchor=\"switch-a-side-between-decks\">Switch a side between decks <span class=\"tag tag--experimental\">experimental<\/span><\/h3>\n<p>The left controls play DECK 1 or DECK 3. The right controls play DECK 2 or DECK 4. Decks 3 and 4 must be ready.<\/p>\n<ul><li>Press <kbd>SHIFT<\/kbd> twice quickly on a side to switch it. The left <kbd>SHIFT<\/kbd> switches between decks 1 and 3, the right <kbd>SHIFT<\/kbd> between decks 2 and 4. These are the presses the XDJ-XZ uses for DJ software.<\/li><li>Or press <kbd>SHORTCUT<\/kbd> and tap the deck under <strong>DECK SELECT<\/strong> <span class=\"tag tag--modern\">modern<\/span>.<\/li><\/ul>\n<p>After a switch the tempo fader does not jump. The deck you switched to keeps its tempo until you move the fader across that deck's value. The same holds when you switch back.<\/p>\n<p>In 2 DECKS the screen follows the sides. A side on deck 3 or 4 shows that deck's waveform, tag and channel, and the screen says where the side went for two seconds, for example <strong>LEFT: DECK 3<\/strong>. In a four-deck view the lanes stay where they are, and a pale blue tag marks the decks the sides control.<\/p>\n<p>If decks 3 and 4 are not running, <kbd>SHIFT<\/kbd> pressed twice does not switch. The screen says <strong>DECK 3 AND 4 NEED THE CH3/CH4 ROUTE<\/strong>. If the route is lost while a side plays deck 3 or 4, both sides go back to decks 1 and 2 and the screen says <strong>DECK 3/4 ROUTE LOST<\/strong>.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-four-decks-7\" data-iface=\"modern\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">SHORTCUT · DECK SELECT<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/9d92fee907c5e01d.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"SHORTCUT with the left side on deck 3.\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"88.500\" data-y=\"13.750\" aria-label=\"1: DECK SELECT\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-7-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"12.500\" data-y=\"97.917\" aria-label=\"2: CONTROL\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-7-2\">2<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>SHORTCUT with the left side on deck 3.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-four-decks-7-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>DECK SELECT<\/b> <span>Each deck row has its switch. Tap 1 or 3 for the left side, 2 or 4 for the right side.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-four-decks-7-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>CONTROL<\/b> <span>In the bottom strip, the decks the sides control carry CONTROL with an arrow.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-four-decks-8\" data-iface=\"modern\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/6c4db278e48987fe.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: SHORTCUT with four decks before the software players report. No DECK SELECT yet\"><img src=\"manual/shots/6c4db278e48987fe.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>SHORTCUT with four decks before the software players report. No DECK SELECT yet<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/9fcb4b1eeba660e1.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: DECK SELECT with both sides on decks 1 and 2\"><img src=\"manual/shots/9fcb4b1eeba660e1.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>DECK SELECT with both sides on decks 1 and 2<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/6b3044b4c3943eec.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: DECK SELECT with both sides on decks 3 and 4\"><img src=\"manual/shots/6b3044b4c3943eec.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>DECK SELECT with both sides on decks 3 and 4<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/4f8afa12e7279ad0.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: The play screen with the left side on deck 3. Its tag and channel read CONTROL\"><img src=\"manual/shots/4f8afa12e7279ad0.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>The play screen with the left side on deck 3. Its tag and channel read CONTROL<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<h3 id=\"m-the-modern-four-deck-screen\" data-anchor=\"the-modern-four-deck-screen\" data-iface=\"modern\">The MODERN four-deck screen <span class=\"tag tag--modern\">modern<\/span><\/h3>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-four-decks-9\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODERN · four decks, number order<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/11eedfd82f73b04d.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"All four decks loaded and playing.\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"79.625\" data-y=\"2.500\" aria-label=\"1: DECKS button\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-9-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"30.000\" data-y=\"40.000\" aria-label=\"2: Lane tag\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-9-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"8.500\" data-y=\"51.250\" aria-label=\"3: VINYL\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-9-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"24.750\" data-y=\"90.833\" aria-label=\"4: Bottom channels\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-9-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"45.250\" data-y=\"72.917\" aria-label=\"5: MASTER\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-9-5\">5<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"6\" data-x=\"97.750\" data-y=\"88.750\" aria-label=\"6: SYNC\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-9-6\">6<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>All four decks loaded and playing.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-four-decks-9-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>DECKS button<\/b> <span>Shows DECKS 1234 or DECKS 3124. Tap it to change the view.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-four-decks-9-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>Lane tag<\/b> <span>The deck's badge, source stick and the key it plays in now, in the key match colours.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-four-decks-9-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>VINYL<\/b> <span>Whether VINYL is on for deck 3 or 4.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-four-decks-9-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>Bottom channels<\/b> <span>The four decks in mixer order 3 1 2 4: time, tempo, range, BPM, hot cues and the whole-track overview.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-four-decks-9-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>MASTER<\/b> <span>The tempo master. A software master reads 3/4 MASTER.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"6\" id=\"f-four-decks-9-6\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">6<\/span><div><b>SYNC<\/b> <span>What SYNC is doing. SYNC 3 means synced to deck 3, BPM 3 deck 3's tempo only, LIMIT a tempo out of reach. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"four-decks\" data-anchor=\"sync-on-decks-3-and-4\">SYNC on decks 3 and 4<\/a>.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<p>Tap a lane of deck 3 or 4 to open its detail panel. It shows the full pad bank, the deck's modes, what SYNC is doing and a whole-track overview you can touch to search. Tap the lane again, or <strong>CLOSE<\/strong>, to close it.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-four-decks-10\" data-iface=\"modern\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/48ba6048f7becd63.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Deck 3 is the deck the encoder and screen act on\"><img src=\"manual/shots/48ba6048f7becd63.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Deck 3 is the deck the encoder and screen act on<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/53a0483825ffa388.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Decks 3 and 4 with no track loaded\"><img src=\"manual/shots/53a0483825ffa388.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Decks 3 and 4 with no track loaded<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/74a00019eaf51198.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Deck 4 is the tempo master and plays a loop\"><img src=\"manual/shots/74a00019eaf51198.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Deck 4 is the tempo master and plays a loop<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/2bffb23d37982b7c.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: A software deck as master. Deck 3 reads 3/4 MASTER and deck 4 reads SYNC 3\"><img src=\"manual/shots/2bffb23d37982b7c.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>A software deck as master. Deck 3 reads 3/4 MASTER and deck 4 reads SYNC 3<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/36852888921f0e60.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: SYNC states. Deck 3 reads BPM 1 and follows deck 1&#x27;s tempo only. Deck 4 reads SYNC 3 and follows deck 3\"><img src=\"manual/shots/36852888921f0e60.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>SYNC states. Deck 3 reads BPM 1 and follows deck 1's tempo only. Deck 4 reads SYNC 3 and follows deck 3<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/1f40f781792e3958.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Mixer order 3 1 2 4\"><img src=\"manual/shots/1f40f781792e3958.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Mixer order 3 1 2 4<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/a0bd695a5a9dfa70.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: ON AIR marks and NEEDLE LOCK, with the playhead on the left\"><img src=\"manual/shots/a0bd695a5a9dfa70.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>ON AIR marks and NEEDLE LOCK, with the playhead on the left<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/e9f41471e42909b3.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Long titles are cut short to fit\"><img src=\"manual/shots/e9f41471e42909b3.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Long titles are cut short to fit<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/71e1c434ffa9e422.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: A read error on deck 3. CANNOT READ THE TRACK, with CHOOSE TRACK\"><img src=\"manual/shots/71e1c434ffa9e422.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>A read error on deck 3. CANNOT READ THE TRACK, with CHOOSE TRACK<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/0b6158978b0120d8.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: GRID ADJUST on deck 4\"><img src=\"manual/shots/0b6158978b0120d8.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>GRID ADJUST on deck 4<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/cf9606d6940a5bb2.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: GRID ADJUST on deck 4 with stem rows on decks 1 and 2\"><img src=\"manual/shots/cf9606d6940a5bb2.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>GRID ADJUST on deck 4 with stem rows on decks 1 and 2<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<p>Stem buttons show only for decks 1 and 2, because decks 3 and 4 have no stems. Each stem layout keeps its place in the four-deck view.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-four-decks-11\" data-iface=\"modern\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/4b12f6c78ec122d6.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Stem rows below decks 1 and 2, full height\"><img src=\"manual/shots/4b12f6c78ec122d6.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Stem rows below decks 1 and 2, full height<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/0f3b467d26a38471.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Stem rows below decks 1 and 2, half height\"><img src=\"manual/shots/0f3b467d26a38471.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Stem rows below decks 1 and 2, half height<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/471a60b9cbc3f82c.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Stem rows outside, full height\"><img src=\"manual/shots/471a60b9cbc3f82c.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Stem rows outside, full height<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/ec793b6ae3515e72.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Stem rows outside, half height\"><img src=\"manual/shots/ec793b6ae3515e72.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Stem rows outside, half height<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/f5e3e8653d982ff5.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Stem rows hidden\"><img src=\"manual/shots/f5e3e8653d982ff5.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Stem rows hidden<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/bafd01ece3e8751f.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Stem pads in the four-deck view\"><img src=\"manual/shots/bafd01ece3e8751f.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Stem pads in the four-deck view<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/154c9ae8aaba8e0a.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Stem pads with BYPASS on deck 2\"><img src=\"manual/shots/154c9ae8aaba8e0a.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Stem pads with BYPASS on deck 2<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/9048674e63b9a582.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Before the stem layout is read\"><img src=\"manual/shots/9048674e63b9a582.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Before the stem layout is read<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<h3 id=\"m-the-classic-four-deck-screen\" data-anchor=\"the-classic-four-deck-screen\" data-iface=\"classic\">The CLASSIC four-deck screen <span class=\"tag tag--classic\">classic<\/span><\/h3>\n<p>CLASSIC keeps the player's own look and adds what four decks need.<\/p>\n<ul><li><strong>Waveforms.<\/strong> The waveform area holds four narrower lanes, one per deck, in the order DECK VIEW chooses. Decks 3 and 4 draw the same 3-band waveform with beat ticks, hot cue flags A to H, the cue point, loops and the playhead.<\/li><li><strong>Side column.<\/strong> The left column has one tag per lane. The tag of a deck a side controls is pale blue with LEFT or RIGHT. Decks 1 and 2 show the analysed key, the playing key and its cents. Decks 3 and 4 show their playing key and its cents the same way, TRACK KEY until they report it, or NOT CONNECTED and SEE THE CARD while they are not running.<\/li><li><strong>Bottom panel.<\/strong> Four channels in mixer order 3 1 2 4. Each shows the deck's title, time, QUANTIZE, tempo and range, AUTO CUE and MT, what SYNC follows, what the pads do, the BPM (orange with MASTER for the master deck) and the whole-track overview. A deck that is not connected shows a dim band with NOT CONNECTED and DECK n WAITS FOR THE LOOPBACK CABLE.<\/li><li><strong>Stem rows<\/strong> are not drawn while four decks show, because there is no room. Your stem layout comes back when you return to two decks. Pressing STEMS meanwhile still steps the saved layout.<\/li><li><strong>2 DECKS<\/strong> shows the decks the sides control. A side on deck 3 or 4 gets a whole half in the player's own style: its waveform, its side tag and its bottom panel.<\/li><\/ul>\n<p>Tap a lane, side tag or channel title of deck 3 or 4 to open its detail panel. Touch the overview in the bottom channel to search the track. NEEDLE LOCK refuses a search while the deck plays.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-load-tracks-onto-decks-3-and-4\" data-anchor=\"load-tracks-onto-decks-3-and-4\">Load tracks onto decks 3 and 4 <span class=\"tag tag--experimental\">experimental<\/span><\/h3>\n<p><kbd>LOAD<\/kbd> on a side loads the highlighted track into the deck that side controls, deck 3 or deck 4 included. In CLASSIC this goes through the player's own browser. In MODERN, tap a track to see a <strong>LOAD<\/strong> chip with one cell per deck, then tap the deck number. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"browse\">Browsing and loading<\/a> for the rest.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-four-decks-12\" data-iface=\"modern\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODERN · load to any deck<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/08a9b4e6c0ebdb11.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"A tapped track with its LOAD cells.\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"56.875\" data-y=\"48.125\" aria-label=\"1: LOAD\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-12-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"76.000\" data-y=\"38.750\" aria-label=\"2: Target deck\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-12-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"12.500\" data-y=\"97.917\" aria-label=\"3: Bottom strip\" aria-describedby=\"f-four-decks-12-3\">3<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>A tapped track with its LOAD cells.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-four-decks-12-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>LOAD<\/b> <span>Tap a deck number to load the track there. LOAD returns to the play screen.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-four-decks-12-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>Target deck<\/b> <span>The blue cell is the deck the screen acts on now.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-four-decks-12-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>Bottom strip<\/b> <span>The four decks in mixer order while you browse.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-four-decks-13\" data-iface=\"modern\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/0bc0c4fc07de1263.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Browsing with four decks. The bottom strip shows all four decks\"><img src=\"manual/shots/0bc0c4fc07de1263.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Browsing with four decks. The bottom strip shows all four decks<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/e200ec7325a15024.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Browsing while the sides control decks 3 and 2\"><img src=\"manual/shots/e200ec7325a15024.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Browsing while the sides control decks 3 and 2<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/d88e39ed62d36369.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Deck 4 with no track. Not Loaded in the strip\"><img src=\"manual/shots/d88e39ed62d36369.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Deck 4 with no track. Not Loaded in the strip<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/971f7bf3c5c11ccd.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: The play screen after a load\"><img src=\"manual/shots/971f7bf3c5c11ccd.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>The play screen after a load<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/48ba6048f7becd63.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: After LOAD on the left side. The track went to the left side&#x27;s deck\"><img src=\"manual/shots/48ba6048f7becd63.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>After LOAD on the left side. The track went to the left side's deck<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/48ba6048f7becd63.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: After LOAD on the right side. The track went to the right side&#x27;s deck\"><img src=\"manual/shots/48ba6048f7becd63.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>After LOAD on the right side. The track went to the right side's deck<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<p>Decks 3 and 4 cannot load a track at a memory point from the CUE/LOOP LIST. The screen says <strong>DECK 3 AND 4 CANNOT LOAD AT A MEMORY POINT<\/strong>.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-info-source-and-utility-with-four-decks\" data-anchor=\"info-source-and-utility-with-four-decks\" data-iface=\"modern\">INFO, SOURCE and UTILITY with four decks <span class=\"tag tag--modern\">modern<\/span><\/h3>\n<p>INFO has a tab for each deck. SOURCE shows which decks use each stick. UTILITY and the other full screens keep a compact strip of all four decks at the bottom.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-four-decks-14\" data-iface=\"modern\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/3cf503c29401eae3.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: INFO with tabs DECK 1 to DECK 4\"><img src=\"manual/shots/3cf503c29401eae3.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>INFO with tabs DECK 1 to DECK 4<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/2552286d9678debe.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: SOURCE. Decks 1 and 2 on USB 1, decks 3 and 4 on USB 2\"><img src=\"manual/shots/2552286d9678debe.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>SOURCE. Decks 1 and 2 on USB 1, decks 3 and 4 on USB 2<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/4dcc1bc4e59c2b3e.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: UTILITY with the four-deck strip at the bottom\"><img src=\"manual/shots/4dcc1bc4e59c2b3e.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>UTILITY with the four-deck strip at the bottom<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/3864cb31e5e31758.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: INFO tabs named PLAYER 3 and PLAYER 4 are other players on the LINK network, not decks 3 and 4\"><img src=\"manual/shots/3864cb31e5e31758.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>INFO tabs named PLAYER 3 and PLAYER 4 are other players on the LINK network, not decks 3 and 4<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/35a65e4e0cc36d73.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: A LINK player with no track loaded\"><img src=\"manual/shots/35a65e4e0cc36d73.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>A LINK player with no track loaded<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<h3 id=\"m-what-decks-3-and-4-can-do\" data-anchor=\"what-decks-3-and-4-can-do\">What decks 3 and 4 can do <span class=\"tag tag--experimental\">experimental<\/span><\/h3>\n<p>Decks 3 and 4 are software players. They follow the player's own controls on the side that controls them. MODS &gt; 4 DECKS shows the current answer for each feature.<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Feature<\/th><th>Decks 1 and 2<\/th><th>Decks 3 and 4<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>Beat jump pads with your own sizes<\/td><td>Yes<\/td><td>Yes, the same sizes and both pages<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Gate cue and smart cue<\/td><td>Yes<\/td><td>Yes<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Waveform colours, key notation, titles<\/td><td>Yes<\/td><td>Yes<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Playing key<\/td><td>Yes<\/td><td>Yes<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Key sync and key shift<\/td><td>Yes<\/td><td>Yes. Both can shift together; new shifts check measured audio headroom.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Stems<\/td><td>Yes, with USB stems set up<\/td><td>No. Decks 3 and 4 have no stems.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>RAM tracks<\/td><td>Yes<\/td><td>Yes, while the loopback cable is connected. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"performance\" data-anchor=\"ram-tracks\">RAM tracks<\/a>.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>On a side that controls deck 3 or 4, these controls work on that deck <span class=\"tag tag--experimental\">experimental<\/span>:<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Control<\/th><th>What it does on deck 3 or 4<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td><kbd>PLAY/PAUSE<\/kbd>, <kbd>CUE<\/kbd><\/td><td>Play and pause, back cue and cue audition. With VINYL on, pause brakes to a stop at the VINYL SPEED ADJUST rate.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><kbd>HOT CUE<\/kbd>, <kbd>BEAT LOOP<\/kbd>, <kbd>SLIP LOOP<\/kbd>, <kbd>BEAT JUMP<\/kbd><\/td><td>Set the pad mode of the software deck. The native deck keeps its own mode.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Pads<\/td><td>Hot cues, beat loops, slip loops and beat jumps, as on decks 1 and 2.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><kbd>LOOP IN<\/kbd>, <kbd>LOOP OUT<\/kbd>, <kbd>RELOOP/EXIT<\/kbd><\/td><td>Manual loops, loop adjustment with the jog, reloop and exit.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><kbd>SLIP<\/kbd>, <kbd>DIRECTION REV<\/kbd>, <kbd>VINYL<\/kbd><\/td><td>Slip, reverse and vinyl mode.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><kbd>TEMPO RANGE<\/kbd>, <kbd>TEMPO RESET<\/kbd>, <kbd>MASTER TEMPO<\/kbd><\/td><td>Tempo range up to WIDE, original speed, and key lock while the tempo moves.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><kbd>SYNC<\/kbd>, <kbd>MASTER<\/kbd><\/td><td>Follow the master deck's tempo, and with QUANTIZE its beat. Make this deck the master. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"four-decks\" data-anchor=\"sync-on-decks-3-and-4\">SYNC on decks 3 and 4<\/a>.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><kbd>SHIFT<\/kbd> + <kbd>SYNC<\/kbd>, <kbd>MASTER TEMPO<\/kbd><\/td><td>KEY SYNC to the master deck, and back to the deck's own key. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"performance\" data-anchor=\"keys-and-key-sync\">Keys and KEY SYNC<\/a>.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><kbd>DECK QUANTIZE<\/kbd><\/td><td>Cue, loop and hot cue points land on the beat. <kbd>DECK QUANTIZE<\/kbd> switches every deck. <kbd>SHIFT<\/kbd> + <kbd>DECK QUANTIZE<\/kbd> switches only this side's deck.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><kbd>MEMORY<\/kbd>, <kbd>DELETE<\/kbd>, <kbd>CUE/LOOP CALL<\/kbd><\/td><td>Store, delete and call memory points.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><kbd>TRACK SEARCH<\/kbd>, <kbd>SEARCH<\/kbd><\/td><td>Previous and next track, and fine search. With AUTO CUE on, the new track waits at its cue. Previous and next follow the list the track was loaded from in MODERN. After a CLASSIC load the deck shows NO SAVED TRACK ORDER, and <kbd>TRACK SEARCH<\/kbd> back returns to the cue.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>Hot cues and memory points you set on decks 3 and 4 are saved on the music stick for those decks only. Decks 1 and 2 and rekordbox do not see them, and the rekordbox export stays unchanged.<\/p>\n<h4 id=\"m-sync-on-decks-3-and-4\" data-anchor=\"sync-on-decks-3-and-4\">SYNC on decks 3 and 4 <span class=\"tag tag--experimental\">experimental<\/span><\/h4>\n<p>Press <kbd>SYNC<\/kbd> and the deck takes the master deck's BPM at once. The SYNC button stays lit for as long as SYNC is on. With QUANTIZE on and a beat grid on both tracks, the deck also locks to the master's beat. Press <kbd>SYNC<\/kbd> again to turn it off.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mx\" data-mx=\"sync-master\" data-mode=\"scenes\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"SYNC on deck 3\"><ol class=\"mx-scenes\"><li data-title=\"Master\" data-v=\"1=MASTER@126.00, 3=@122.00\"><b>Master<\/b> <span>Deck 1 is the tempo master. Deck 3 plays at its own tempo, with SYNC off.<\/span><\/li><li data-title=\"SYNC\" data-v=\"1=MASTER@126.00, 3=SYNC 1@126.00, lock\"><b>SYNC<\/b> <span>Press <kbd>SYNC<\/kbd> on deck 3. It takes the master's BPM at once and reads SYNC 1. With QUANTIZE on and a beat grid on both tracks, it also locks to the master's beat.<\/span><\/li><li data-title=\"Tempo only\" data-v=\"1=MASTER@126.00, 3=BPM 1@126.00\"><b>Tempo only<\/b> <span>With QUANTIZE off, only the tempo follows, and deck 3 reads BPM 1.<\/span><\/li><\/ol><\/div>\n<p>If the beats drift apart, press <kbd>SYNC<\/kbd> off and on again. With QUANTIZE on, every engage snaps to the nearest position at the selected beat value, even for a small drift. The beat value can be 1, 1/2, 1/4 or 1/8 beat. With QUANTIZE off, only the tempo follows.<\/p>\n<ul><li>The tempo follows even when the master or the synced deck is paused. If the beat position is available, the paused deck aligns once. If it is unavailable, alignment happens as soon as it can be read. Continuous beat lock resumes when both decks play.<\/li><li>A pause, a jump, a loop or a new master never turns SYNC off. The deck follows again on its own, with no second press.<\/li><li>Bending or scratching takes control of the deck. When you let go, QUANTIZE snaps it back into alignment as soon as beat timing is available.<\/li><li>The tempo fader does not move the deck while SYNC is on.<\/li><\/ul>\n<p>The bottom channel, the lane and the detail panel say what SYNC is doing:<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Shown<\/th><th>What it means<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>SYNC 1 to SYNC 4<\/td><td>SYNC is on and follows that deck.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>BPM 1 to BPM 4<\/td><td>Only the tempo can follow that deck: QUANTIZE is off, a track has no beat grid, a loop is running, or the master's beat position is not available.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>MASTER<\/td><td>This deck is the tempo master.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>3/4 MASTER<\/td><td>This deck is the master for decks 3 and 4 only.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>LIMIT<\/td><td>The master's tempo is out of this deck's reach. The deck keeps its last tempo.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>EXT MASTER<\/td><td>The master is another player on the LINK network, which decks 3 and 4 cannot follow.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>NO BPM<\/td><td>The track has no BPM to sync with. Analyse it in rekordbox.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>The detail panel adds a line about the reason, for example:<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Detail panel<\/th><th>What it means<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>SYNC ON / FOLLOWING DECK 1<\/td><td>The deck follows deck 1.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>SYNC ON / TEMPO MATCHED, PAUSED / TEMPO MATCHED<\/td><td>The tempo matches. The beat locks once both decks play.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>BPM SYNC / MASTER PAUSED, BPM SYNC / DECK PAUSED<\/td><td>One of the two decks is paused. The tempo follows, and the beat locks once both play.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>BPM SYNC / NO BEAT GRID<\/td><td>A track has no beat grid, so only the tempo follows.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>BPM SYNC / LOOP ACTIVE<\/td><td>A loop is running, so only the tempo follows until it ends.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>BPM SYNC / BEAT POSITION UNAVAILABLE<\/td><td>The master's beat position cannot be read, so only the tempo follows.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>BPM SYNC / QUANTIZE OFF<\/td><td>QUANTIZE is off, so only the tempo follows.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>SYNC ON / JOG CONTROL<\/td><td>You are bending or scratching. SYNC picks up again when you let go.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>NO MASTER / TEMPO UNCHANGED<\/td><td>No deck is master. The deck keeps its tempo and follows as soon as there is one.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>MASTER CLOCK UNAVAILABLE / LAST TEMPO RETAINED<\/td><td>The master's tempo cannot be read right now. The deck keeps the last tempo.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>SYNC TEMPO LIMIT / LAST TEMPO RETAINED<\/td><td>The master's tempo is out of reach.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>EXTERNAL MASTER / SYNC SOURCE UNAVAILABLE<\/td><td>A LINK player is master.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>TRACK BPM UNAVAILABLE / SYNC ON<\/td><td>The track has no BPM.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<h3 id=\"m-limits\" data-anchor=\"limits\">Limits<\/h3>\n<ul><li>Decks 1 and 2 must be stopped or paused while decks 3 and 4 start.<\/li><li>Keep the music stick connected while you play. Decks 3 and 4 read from it all the time.<\/li><li>Decks 3 and 4 play WAV, AIFF, FLAC, MP3 and Ogg Vorbis files. AAC and M4A files do not play on decks 3 and 4.<\/li><li>A deck 3 or 4 master reads MASTER when decks 1 and 2 can follow it too, and 3/4 MASTER when it drives decks 3 and 4 only.<\/li><li>When the master stops, MASTER passes to the next playing deck in deck order. After deck 3 comes deck 4, then decks 1 and 2. After deck 4 come decks 1 and 2, then deck 3. A master set by another player over LINK is never taken.<\/li><li>Some lamps on the player do not yet light as they do for decks 1 and 2. The beat loop and slip loop pad colours are provisional.<\/li><li>Four decks, the handover of MASTER between native and software decks, and scratching on decks 3 and 4 are experimental in this version.<\/li><\/ul>\n<p>If something goes wrong, the card or the 4 DECKS page names the state. <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"troubleshooting\">Messages and troubleshooting<\/a> lists every notice.<\/p>";
